  {
   "id": "concept2",
   "type": "concept",
   "title": {
    "en": "Performance of the half-wave rectifier"
   },
   "body": {
    "en": "For an ideal diode, $I_{dc} = I_m/\\pi$, $V_{dc} = V_m/\\pi \\approx 0.318V_m$ and $I_{rms} = I_m/2$. The ripple factor is $r = \\sqrt{(I_{rms}/I_{dc})^2 - 1} = 1.21$, the maximum efficiency is 40.6 %, the peak inverse voltage on the diode is V_m and the transformer utilisation factor is about 0.287. With a real silicon diode, V_m is reduced by about 0.7 V."
   },
   "points": [
    {
     "en": "V_dc = V_m/π, I_rms = I_m/2"
    },
    {
     "en": "Ripple factor 1.21, efficiency 40.6 %"
    },
    {
     "en": "PIV = V_m"
    }
   ],
   "narration": {
    "en": "The d.c. output is V m by pi. The ripple factor is 1.21, the maximum efficiency is 40.6 percent and the diode must withstand V m in reverse.",
    "kn": "ನೇರ ಔಟ್‌ಪುಟ್ Vm/π. ತರಂಗಾಂಶ ಅಂಶ 1.21, ಗರಿಷ್ಠ ದಕ್ಷತೆ 40.6 ಶೇಕಡಾ, ಡಯೋಡ್ ಹಿಮ್ಮುಖದಲ್ಲಿ Vm ತಡೆಯಬೇಕು."
   },
   "formula": "V_{dc} = \\frac{V_m}{\\pi},\\quad I_{rms} = \\frac{I_m}{2},\\quad r = 1.21,\\quad \\eta_{max} = 40.6\\%"
  },
